{"id":45,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield","X","LeafGreen","Blue","Red"],"text":"The larger its petals, the more toxic pollen it contains. Its big head is heavy and hard to hold up."},{"games":["Sword","Y","HeartGold","Gold"],"text":"It has the world’s largest petals. With every step, the petals shake out heavy clouds of toxic pollen."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!","Yellow"],"text":"Flaps its broad flower petals to scatter its poisonous pollen. The flapping sound is very loud."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Sapphire"],"text":"Vileplume has the world’s largest petals. They are used to attract prey that are then doused with toxic spores. Once the prey are immobilized, this Pokémon catches and devours them."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"Vileplume’s toxic pollen triggers atrocious allergy attacks. That’s why it is advisable never to approach any attractive flowers in a jungle, however pretty they may be."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"Its petals are the largest in the world. As it walks, it scatters extremely allergenic pollen."},{"games":["SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"The bud bursts into bloom with a bang. It then starts scattering allergenic, poisonous pollen."},{"games":["FireRed"],"text":"Its petals are the largest in the world. It fiendishly scatters allergy-causing pollen from its petals."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"In seasons when it produces more pollen, the air around a VILEPLUME turns yellow with the powder as it walks. The pollen is highly toxic and causes paralysis."},{"games":["Crystal"],"text":"By shaking its big petals, it scatters toxic pollen into the air, turning the air yellow."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Chlorophyll","hidden":false,"description":"Boosts the Pokémon's Speed stat in harsh sunlight."},{"name":"Effect Spore","hidden":true,"description":"Contact with the Pokémon may inflict poison, sleep, or paralysis on the attacker."}],"eggGroups":["Grass"],"genderRate":4,